<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adriaan van Jaarsveld</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1745–1801</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adriaan van Jaarsveld was a frontier farmer and commando leader on the eastern border of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a>, known for campaigns against the Xhosa. In February 1795 he and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marthinus-prinsloo">Marthinus Prinsloo</a> led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghers">burghers</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/graaff-reinet">Graaff-Reinet</a> in expelling the landdrost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honoratus-maynier">Honoratus Maynier</a> and declaring a short-lived republic. He was later arrested for forgery and rebellion and died in prison in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-town">Cape Town</a>.</p></div>
